<h1>Security</h1><p class="meta">Last updated October 8, 2026</p><p>Protecting payment data is the foundation of everything we build. This page summarizes how we safeguard the Services.</p><ul><li><strong>Card data stays out of our systems.</strong> Card numbers are captured by PCI DSS validated payment providers through secure fields and certified devices. AmpliRail receives tokens, never full card numbers or security codes.</li><li><strong>Encryption.</strong> Data is encrypted in transit with TLS 1.2 or higher and at rest with AES-256. Sensitive identity data, such as tax and government ID numbers, is encrypted field by field and stored separately, and is shown masked (for example, last four digits only).</li><li><strong>Access control.</strong> Multi-factor authentication for all administrative access, least-privilege roles, automatic session timeouts, and an audit trail of administrative actions.</li><li><strong>Infrastructure.</strong> Hosted in isolated environments with private networks, firewalls and web application protection. Databases are not reachable from the internet.</li><li><strong>Monitoring and response.</strong> Continuous logging and alerting, with a documented incident response plan.</li><li><strong>Resilience.</strong> Encrypted backups kept in a separate location and tested regularly.</li><li><strong>Compliance.</strong> Our payment providers are PCI DSS Level 1 service providers. AmpliRail&#x27;s own PCI DSS Level 1 assessment is in progress.</li><li><strong>Responsible disclosure.</strong> Found a vulnerability? Email <a href="mailto:security@amplipay.ai">security@amplipay.ai</a>. Please do not access other users&#x27; data or disrupt the Services. We will respond promptly and will not pursue good-faith research that follows these rules.</li></ul><p class="note">This page describes our security program and is not a guarantee or warranty. No system can be completely secure.</p>
